// MODELDEF.aemain -- GENERATED by tools/gen_aedual_modeldef.py (2026-10-23). Do not edit by hand.
//
// The MAIN gun's hand while DUAL WIELDING, ported from BD22 1.92's RSQ_DualHands
// (zscript/rsq/dualhands.zs) which the pack had only half-ported.
//
// Why this file exists: hw_weapon.cpp GetWeaponPosition3D sends every layer whose caller is
// not the ready weapon through the OFF-HAND weapon's psprite, and hw_weapon.cpp:943-948 then
// looks ModifyBobLayer3D up on THAT actor's class. While a gun is in the off hand that actor
// is an AE_Off_* copy, which is DECORATE and cannot override a ZScript virtual (verified: a
// ZScript class may not inherit a DECORATE actor -- "unknown base class"). So the hook is
// nulled for EVERY such layer, including the main hand on RSQ_GunSide. BD22's answer is not
// to fight it: draw each gun's hand as a layer CALLED BY THAT GUN, with the hook baked into
// Offset, and clear the layers that can no longer be placed.
//
// These are the blocks for the MAIN gun's hand (layer RSQ_Layers.MAINGUN), bound to each base
// gun class. Offset = (0 + GunHook.x, -24 + GunHook.z, -10 + GunHook.y) -- y and z SWAPPED,
// because models.cpp RenderHUDModel feeds matrix-y from Offset's THIRD number and matrix-z from
// its SECOND, while the ModifyBobLayer3D hook goes in as (X, Y, Z) straight. Same bake as the
// AE_Off_* hand blocks in MODELDEF.aedual. Only guns whose GunRot is (0,0,0) are here: a
// rotation cannot be baked into Offset, so RSQ_DualHands skips the rest (smartguns, satchels,
// knives) exactly as BD22 skips its axe and chainsaw.
//
// Regenerate with:  python tools/gen_aedual_modeldef.py --emit-main

Model M240Flamethrower_3D
{
	Path "models/rsq"
	Model 0 "hand.md3"
	Skin 0 "hand.png"
	Scale -1.0 1.0 1.0
	Offset 0.000 -24.000 -10.000	// GunHook (0.000 0.000 0.000) baked 2026-10-23 (y/z swapped)
FrameIndex RQGS A 0 0	// Ermac hand.md3 frame 0
	FrameIndex RQGS B 0 1	// Ermac hand.md3 frame 1
	FrameIndex RQGS C 0 2	// Ermac hand.md3 frame 19
	FrameIndex RQGS D 0 3	// Ermac hand.md3 frame 29
